{"books":[{"id":"1497","title":"Bhagavad Gita","description":"The content of the text is a conversation between Krishna and Arjuna taking place on the battlefield of Kurukshetra just prior to the start of a climactic war. Responding to Arjuna's confusion and moral dilemma, Krishna explains to Arjuna his duties as a warrior and Prince and elaborates on a number of different Yogic and Vedantic philosophies, with examples and analogies. This has led to the Gita often being described as a concise guide to Hindu philosophy and also as a practical, self-contained guide to life. During the discourse, Krishna reveals his identity as the Supreme Being Himself (Bhagavan), blessing Arjuna with an awe-inspiring glimpse of His divine absolute form. (Wikipedia)","url_text_source":"https:\/\/www.bartleby.com\/br\/04504.html","language":"English","copyright_year":"1909","num_sections":"19","url_rss":"https:\/\/librivox.org\/rss\/1497","url_zip_file":"https:\/\/archive.org\/compress\/bhagavad_gita_0803_librivox\/formats=64KBPS MP3&file=\/bhagavad_gita_0803_librivox.zip","url_project":"https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Bhagavad_gita","url_librivox":"https:\/\/librivox.org\/bhagavad-gita-by-sir-edwin-arnold\/","url_other":"","totaltime":"2:54:53","totaltimesecs":10493,"authors":[{"id":"221","first_name":"","last_name":"Unknown","dob":"","dod":""}],"url_iarchive":"https:\/\/www.archive.org\/details\/bhagavad_gita_0803_librivox","sections":[{"id":"146052","section_number":"0","title":"Introduction","listen_url":"https:\/\/www.archive.org\/download\/bhagavad_gita_0803_librivox\/bhagavadgita_00_64kb.mp3","language":"English","playtime":"183","file_name":null,"readers":[{"reader_id":"1392","display_name":"Chris Masterson"}]},{"id":"146053","section_number":"1","title":"Chapter 1: Of the Distress of Arjuna","listen_url":"https:\/\/www.archive.org\/download\/bhagavad_gita_0803_librivox\/bhagavadgita_01_64kb.mp3","language":"English","playtime":"580","file_name":null,"readers":[{"reader_id":"